VeridianOS: binutils libtool flags without libtool notes

ld's libdep plugin is linked with "-rpath /nowhere" on top of the
"-rpath $(bfdplugindir)" automake gives every installed libtool library,
so libtool warned "ignoring multiple -rpath's for a libtool library" and,
at install, "remember to run 'libtool --finish /nowhere'". The flag goes
(the testplug libraries, which are not installed, keep theirs): the
plugin is linked for, and installed into, bfd-plugins as before. With
the first -rpath gone, libdep.la's libdir is the real install directory,
so a "make install" without DESTDIR would now run "libtool --finish"
there (ldconfig -n and a banner); build-musl-toolchain.sh installs with
LIBTOOLFLAGS=--no-finish, which keeps the installed files and the
install steps as before.

libsframe and libctf pass -version-info whether they are installed
libraries (--enable-install-libbfd) or not; for the internal convenience
libraries of an ordinary build libtool ignores it and warns
("-version-info/-version-number is ignored for convenience libraries").
The version is now given only to the installed libraries.

Both Makefile.am and the generated Makefile.in are changed (binutils
builds without maintainer mode, so automake does not run).

--- a/ld/Makefile.am
+++ b/ld/Makefile.am
@@ -719,7 +719,7 @@
 bfdplugindir = $(libdir)/bfd-plugins
 bfdplugin_LTLIBRARIES = libdep.la
 libdep_la_SOURCES = libdep_plugin.c
-libdep_la_LDFLAGS = -no-undefined -rpath /nowhere -module -avoid-version
+libdep_la_LDFLAGS = -no-undefined -module -avoid-version
 libdep_la_LINK = $(LIBTOOL) $(AM_V_lt) --tag=CC $(AM_LIBTOOLFLAGS) \
 	--tag=disable-static \
 	$(LIBTOOLFLAGS) --mode=link $(CCLD) $(AM_CFLAGS) $(CFLAGS) \
--- a/ld/Makefile.in
+++ b/ld/Makefile.in
@@ -1060,7 +1060,7 @@
